A GIF version for chat and Discord: <a href="./press-demo.gif">press-demo.gif</a>.</p>

<h2>What it does</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Photograph a character sheet &mdash; <strong>typed, printed, PDF, or handwritten</strong> &mdash; and get back an editable digital sheet.</li>
  <li><strong>Any game system.</strong> It reads the sheet in front of it rather than assuming a ruleset, so it is not tied to one game.</li>
  <li>One scan handles <strong>up to ten pages of a single character</strong>, not just one page.</li>
  <li>Every field is editable by hand afterwards.</li>
  <li>Exports a <strong>print-ready PDF</strong> of the finished sheet.</li>
  <li>Characters sync to your account, so they follow you between devices.</li>
</ul>

<h2>What it does not do &mdash; the honest limits</h2>
<div class="box">
<ul>
  <li><strong>It needs an internet connection to scan.</strong> The reading happens on a server, not on the phone. Everything else &mdash; viewing and editing your saved characters &mdash; works without it.</li>
  <li><strong>Messy handwriting produces mistakes.</strong> It is a reader, not a mind. Expect to glance over a scanned sheet and correct a field or two, the same way you would proofread a photocopy.</li>
  <li><strong>A dense multi-page sheet takes a couple of minutes,</strong> not a couple of seconds. Ten pages of a crowded Pathfinder character is real work.</li>
  <li><strong>One scan, one character.</strong> It will not digitise a whole party in a single pass.</li>
</ul>
</div>
<p class="eff">We would rather you knew these going in than discovered them mid-review.</p>

<h2>How the scan works</h2>
<p>Sheetmancer uses a machine-vision model to <strong>read</strong> a photo of a character sheet you already own and
place that text into editable fields. That is the only thing the technology does here: read a page you chose to
photograph, the same job a document scanner or a visual-lookup app does.</p>
<p>It does <strong>not</strong> generate characters, art, rules, or lore. It does not write anything that was not
already on your paper. Every field is editable and correctable by hand afterwards. No generative AI was used for
the app's own artwork, icons, store listing, or written copy.</p>
<p>How your data is handled is set out in full in the <a href="./privacy.html">Sheetmancer Privacy Policy</a>,
and you can delete your account and its data from inside the app at any time
(<a href="./delete-account.html">instructions here</a>).</p>

